FINAL ANSWER:
## 🚌 Bus Factor Analysis (surviving-code ownership)
Period: all history | Generated: 2026-10-24

I used `git blame` instead of the skill's per-file commit counts. It counts the lines that exist today and who last meaningfully wrote them. I ignored whitespace changes and moved or copied lines. I also excluded the latest commit (`62628c0`, the 4-space and double-quote reformat). That commit rewrote about 1,000 lines across `test/test.js` and the other test files and would otherwise have been credited with them. I did not run the contributor-analyzer agent or the importance step, because the repo is only 18 tracked files.

### Project-level bus factor: 2

Troy Goode and Douglas Christopher Wilson together own 72% of all lines (1,412 of 1,968) and 90% of the code in `lib/` and `test/` (1,072 of 1,204). Losing those two would leave most of the code without a maintainer who wrote it.

### Who owns what today

| Author | Surviving lines (all files) | Share | Last commit |
|---|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode | 804 | 41% | 2026-04-10 |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 608 | 31% | **2021-09-07** |
| Íñigo Marquínez Prado | 95 | 5% | not checked |
| Jon Church | 72 | 4% | not checked |
| Sebastian Beltran | 67 | 3% | not checked |
| Ulises Gascón | 52 | 3% | 2026-01-22 |
| Ignacio Mangas | 44 | 2% | not checked |
| About 40 others | 226 | 11% | not checked |

Most of the smaller owners hold CI config (Íñigo, Sebastian, Ignacio, Ulises) or README text (Jon Church).

### Ownership by file

| File | Primary owner | Share | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `lib/index.js` (the only runtime code) | Troy Goode | 67% (159 of 238 lines) | Douglas owns 9%, and about 17 others own the rest. |
| `test/test.js` | Douglas 39%, Troy 36% | — | About 10 other contributors. |
| `test/vary.js`, `test/issue-2.js`, `test/example-app.js`, `test/error-response.js` | Troy Goode | 83–100% | Douglas owns the remainder. |
| `package.json`, `HISTORY.md`, `.eslintrc.yml` | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 56–100% | |
| `.github/workflows/*`, `dependabot.yml` | Íñigo, Sebastian, Ulises, Ignacio | — | Spread across them, with no single owner. |
| `README.md` | Troy Goode | 22% | Widely spread. |

### Risk areas

| Area | Sole or primary owner | Active? | Risk |
|---|---|---|---|
| `lib/index.js` | Troy Goode (67%) | ✅ Active (April 2026) | **HIGH**. It is the only runtime file and has one dominant author. |
| `test/vary.js`, `test/issue-2.js`, `test/example-app.js`, `test/error-response.js` | Troy Goode (83–100%) | ✅ Active | MEDIUM |
| `package.json`, `HISTORY.md`, `.eslintrc.yml` | Douglas Christopher Wilson | ❌ Inactive since 2021 | MEDIUM. This is release and config knowledge held by someone who has left. |
| `test/test.js` | Douglas 39%, Troy 36% | Troy active, Douglas not | MEDIUM. Troy is the only active large owner. |
| CI workflows | Several people | Partly | LOW |

### Heat map

```
repo/
├── lib/       [███████░░░] 🔴 Bus factor 1 (Troy 67%)
├── test/      [██████░░░░] 🟡 Bus factor 2 (Troy 56%, Douglas 33%, Douglas inactive)
├── .github/   [███░░░░░░░] 🟢 Bus factor 3+ (spread across four people)
├── README.md  [██░░░░░░░░] 🟢 Widely distributed
└── package.json, HISTORY.md [█████░░░░░] 🟡 Mostly Douglas (inactive)
```

### Recommendations

1. **Immediate:** Have someone besides Troy review changes to `lib/index.js`, and document why it works the way it does. It is small (238 lines), so this is cheap.
2. **Short-term:** Record Douglas's release and `package.json` conventions somewhere, since they're no longer around to ask.
3. **Ongoing:** Pair Troy with another maintainer on the `test/` helper files that only Troy has touched.

### Caveats

- Blame credits the last author to touch a line. If a line was reworded by someone else, the original author loses credit.
- Authors are counted by name, so the same person under two names (for example "Alejandro Caravaca Puchades" and "alex94puchades") is counted as two.
- I checked last-commit dates only for the top four authors. Whether Íñigo, Jon, Sebastian and Ignacio are still active is unknown.
- Troy Goode's last commit is dated 2026-04-10, so "active" means active within about six months. That is outside the skill's 90-day window, and by that stricter standard Troy would also count as inactive.

